w: 1.~When I sur- vey _ the won- drous cross On which the Prince _ _ of glo- ry died, _ _ My rich- est gain _ I count but _ loss, _ _ And pour con- _ tempt on _ all my pride.
w: 2.~For- bid it, Lord, _ that I should boast, Save in the death _ _ of Christ my God! _ _ All the vain things _ that charm me _ most, _ _ I sac- ri- _ fice them _ to His blood.
w: 3.~See from His head, _ His hands, His feet, Sor- row and love _ _ flow min- gled down! _ _ Did e'er such love _ and sor- row _ meet, _ _ Or thorns com- _ pose so _ rich a crown?
w: 4.~His dy- ing crim- _ son, like a robe, Spreads o'er His bo- _ _ dy on the tree; _ _ Then I am dead _ to all the _ globe, _ _ And all the _ globe is _ dead to me.
w: 5.~Were the whole realm _ of na- ture mine, That were a pre- _ _ sent far too small; _ _ Love so a- ma- _ zing, so di- _ vine, _ _ De- mands my _ soul, my _ life, my all.
